%!PS
% SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 EfterScript contributors
% SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
% oracle: colour
% Scenario: a lattice mesh from a hexadecimal string. A type 5 shading
% gives two rows of three vertices at eight bits per coordinate and
% per component, each vertex x y r g b in five bytes, the coordinates
% decoded over the byte range; the data goes to the PDF as it was
% given.
gsave
100 300 translate
<< /ShadingType 5 /ColorSpace /DeviceRGB
   /BitsPerCoordinate 8 /BitsPerComponent 8 /VerticesPerRow 3
   /Decode [0 255 0 255 0 1 0 1 0 1]
   /DataSource <
     0000 ff0000  640a 00ff00  c800 0000ff
     0064 ffff00  645a 00ffff  c864 ff00ff > >> shfill
grestore
showpage
